import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Editorial Policy & Fact-Checking Standards — Rent Free News" description="Rent Free News editorial standards, verification methodology, non-partisanship pledge, corrections policy, and editorial contact details.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <div class="kicker text-brand-600">Trust & Transparency</div>
    <h1 class="font-display font-black text-[34px] sm:text-[42px] tracking-[-0.02em] mt-1">Editorial Policy & Fact-Checking Standards</h1>
    
    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert font-serif mt-6 space-y-6">
      <p class="font-sans text-[17px] text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
        Rent Free News is an independent media-accountability newsroom founded on a single premise: <strong>viral claims belong on top, primary data belongs below, and the receipts must be verified visibly.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>1. Our Mission & Editorial Scope</h2>
      <p>
        In an era dominated by algorithmic virality, misleading headlines, and recycled commentary, Rent Free News cuts through noise by cross-examining viral narratives against documented primary sources. We cover breaking tech policy, national affairs, cybersecurity incidents, labor market restructuring, and cultural debates through a strict claim-versus-data editorial structure.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The Multi-Step Fact-Checking Methodology</h2>
      <p>Every article published across our editorial desks adheres to a four-stage verification protocol before going live:</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-sans text-[15px]">
        <li><strong>Archival of Viral Claims:</strong> We capture, screenshot, and archive viral statements, social posts, or press reports to evaluate the original context and reach before claims can be retroactively edited or deleted.</li>
        <li><strong>Primary Source Retrieval:</strong> We do not rely on second-hand reporting, anonymous aggregators, or unsourced social media screenshots. Every claim is compared against original primary records: official court filings, corporate SEC 10-K/10-Q disclosures, open-source telemetry logs, regulatory gazettes, scientific datasets, or unedited video timestamps.</li>
        <li><strong>Direct Attribution & Subject Verification:</strong> When covering independent creators, developers, researchers, or local witnesses, we seek direct quotes with permission, provide draft review for quotes, and link back directly to primary creators.</li>
        <li><strong>Standardized Public Verdicts:</strong> Every investigation concludes with a transparent editorial verdict (<em>True with context</em>, <em>Misleading — Missing Context</em>, <em>False — with context</em>, <em>Missing Context</em>, or <em>Explainer</em>), accompanied by a "Why It Matters" stakes briefing.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>3. Editorial Independence & Non-Partisanship</h2>
      <p>
        Rent Free News is independently funded and editorial decisions are made free from external interference:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 font-sans text-[15px]">
        <li>We accept no funding, donations, or grants from political parties, political action committees (PACs), or government agencies.</li>
        <li>Editorial staff operate under strict conflict-of-interest guidelines: journalists may not hold financial stakes in companies they cover or participate in partisan campaigns.</li>
        <li>Verdicts and investigation selections are never for sale. All commercial partnerships, sponsored sections, or display advertisements are clearly demarcated from independent news reporting.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Anti-Slop & Human Quality Control</h2>
      <p>
        All articles published on Rent Free News are crafted and reviewed by human writers and editors under rigorous editorial slop budgets. We strictly ban generic corporate filler, artificial intelligence hallucinations, and unverified rumors. Visuals accompanying articles are dedicated editorial illustrations conforming to our published broadsheet vector aesthetic.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Transparent Corrections Policy</h2>
      <p>
        Accuracy is our foremost obligation, but when an error occurs, our policy is to correct it swiftly, visibly, and without stealth updates. Factual errors are updated directly in the text with a prominent correction note detailing what was changed, when, and why. Readers can review our corrections record and report errors anytime through our dedicated <a href="/corrections/" class="underline font-semibold">Corrections Portal</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Contact the Editorial Desk</h2>
      <p>
        We encourage tips, documentation leaks, academic papers, and fact-checking suggestions from readers, researchers, and journalists.
      </p>
      <div class="rounded-[10px] border border-hairline dark:border-zinc-800 bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 p-5 font-sans text-[14px] not-prose space-y-2">
        <div><strong>Editor-in-Chief & Editorial Inquiries:</strong> <a href="mailto:editor@rentfreenews.com" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">editor@rentfreenews.com</a></div>
        <div><strong>General Newsroom & Tips:</strong> <a href="mailto:desk@rentfreenews.com" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">desk@rentfreenews.com</a></div>
        <div><strong>Corrections Desk:</strong> <a href="/corrections/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">rentfreenews.com/corrections</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

